To hunt for bugs on an Application Programming Interface (API) using ffuf like the top 1% of researchers, you have to throw out standard web-fuzzing rules. APIs don't usually serve HTML pages—they serve structured text (JSON/XML) and rely on strict HTTP verbs (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH).
Here is the master playbook for elite API reconnaissance and anomaly discovery.
